<item>
 <title>From Madrid to the sky</title>
 <link>http://2012.drupalcamp.es/en/madrid-sky-170</link>
 <description>
  &lt;div class=&quot;field-image&quot;&gt;
    &lt;img typeof=&quot;foaf:Image&quot; src=&quot;http://2012.drupalcamp.es/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/field/image/madrid.jpg&quot; width=&quot;275&quot; height=&quot;183&quot; alt=&quot;Madrid at night&quot; /&gt;  &lt;/div&gt;

  &lt;div class=&quot;field-body&quot;&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Madrid, Spanish capitol since 1562, is the geographic centre of the Iberic Peninsula. It&#039;s height, and the fact of being over a plateau and surrounded by mountains defines its weather with warm summers and not so cold winters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a capitol, it is a very monumental city, with a very popular hearth centre built during the Habsburg reign. &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.museodelprado.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;The Prado Museum&lt;/a&gt; is considered one of the best galleries all over the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But Madrid is also a city that never sleeps. It has a huge amount of bars, cafes, theatres, discos which open literally all night. Therefore, do not be surprised if you get caught at a traffic jam at 4am in the night.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here are some useful links to get you started:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://todosobremadrid.com&quot;&gt;General information about Madrid&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://pinterest.com/search/?q=madrid&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Madrid&#039;s Pinterest&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.flickr.com/search/?q=madrid&amp;amp;f=hp&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Madrid at Flickr&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;  &lt;/div&gt;
